<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barakah nuclear power plant</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Barakah nuclear power plant, in the Al Dhafra region of western Abu Dhabi, is the first nuclear power station in the Arab world. Built by a South Korean consortium led by KEPCO, its four reactors were connected to the grid between 2020 and 2024, and together they supply about a quarter of the electricity of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barakah-nuclear-power-plant.jpg" alt="Barakah nuclear power plant" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wikiemirati · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barakah_nuclear_power_plant.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
